Pending workbench and token without RBAC, position silently omitted — no position data, no error indicators\n- Validation finding on default RBAC availability documented; behavior correct either way\n- UI remains responsive with integration (performance)\n\nHLR: P1-1. Depends on the state-driven status model (plain terms: \"depends on the state-driven workload status model work, which determines pending state and the status display the position renders into\").\n\nE003 body:\n\nTitle: Kueue context indicators on project details and workbenches overview\n\nDescription: Adds two conditional UI indicators communicating Kueue management context: a positive indicator on the project details page when the namespace is Kueue-managed, and an anomaly indicator on workbenches in Kueue-managed namespaces that are NOT managed by Kueue.\n\nScope:\n- Project details page: positive indicator (info banner/badge/label — placeholder treatment pending UX finalization) when namespace has kueue.openshift.io/managed=true\n- Workbenches overview: anomaly indicator only on workbenches in Kueue-managed namespaces missing the kueue.x-k8s.io/queue-name label (workload matching via existing buildWorkloadMapForNotebooks); absent on Kueue-managed workloads; steady-state workloads get no redundant \"managed by Kueue\" badge\n- Warning (never blocking) about missing queue labels\n- Conditional display: indicators appear only in Kueue-managed namespaces; no change otherwise\n\nACs:\n- Positive indicator present in DOM when namespace label exists, absent when not\n- Anomaly indicator present only on non-Kueue workloads in Kueue-managed namespaces, absent on Kueue-managed workloads\n- Placeholder visual treatment replaceable when finalized UX design arrives\n\nHLR: P0-3, P0-4.\n\nE004 body:\n\nTitle: HardwareProfile form and popover Kueue enhancements\n\nDescription: Hardens HardwareProfile-related UI for Kueue contexts: popover fallback for GitOps-managed notebooks with directly-applied queue labels, LocalQueue name validation in the admin form, an explanatory info indicator on the filtered HP dropdown, and a non-blocking warning when a referenced LocalQueue doesn't exist at workbench creation.\n\nScope:\n- HP details popover: when no HP scheduling data matches, fall back to reading kueue.x-k8s.io/queue-name from the notebook's own labels; resolve cluster queue name from project's LocalQueue list; indicate source (\"applied directly\" vs \"via hardware profile\")\n- HP admin form: validate LocalQueue name against k8sNameRegex (/^[a-z0-9]([-a-z0-9]*[a-z0-9])?$/); cannot validate existence (HP cluster-scoped, LQ namespace-scoped)\n- Workbench creation: if specified LocalQueue doesn't exist in namespace, show dismissible warning — not an error; never block creation\n- HP dropdown in workbench creation form (Kueue-managed namespace): keep strict filtering to queue-enabled profiles; add info icon/tooltip explaining why\n\nACs: strategy ACs 7, 8, 9, 11 (popover source indicator; inline validation error referencing Kubernetes name format; dismissible non-blocking LQ-not-found warning; tooltip/info icon adjacent to dropdown).\n\nHLR: P1-2, P1-3, P1-4.\n\nE005 body:\n\nTitle: UX visual treatment for Kueue indicators and status messaging\n\nDescription: UXD deliverable (RHOAIUX-7470): finalized visual treatments for the positive Kueue indicator on project details, the workload anomaly indicator, the HP dropdown info indicator, and content review of status messaging. Engineering proceeds with placeholders in parallel; this deliverable replaces them.\n\nScope:\n- Decide form of positive Kueue indicator (info banner vs badge vs label) for project details\n- Visual design for anomaly indicator on non-Kueue workloads\n- Visual treatment for HP dropdown info indicator\n- Content review collaboration for status message overrides\n- Deliver finalized specs ready for implementation hand-off\n\nACs:\n- Finalized visual treatment for positive indicator delivered (decision among banner/badge/label)\n- Anomaly indicator and dropdown info indicator designs delivered\n- Deliverables structured to replace engineering placeholder treatments without rework of conditional logic\n\nHLR: supports P0-3, P0-4, P1-4 (design deliverables that finalize treatment of these requirements).\n\nHmm — HLR traceability \"which strategy HLRs this epic covers\". E005 covers (partially) P0-3, P0-4, P1-4. OK.\n\nE006 body:\n\nTitle: Human-friendly status message microcopy for Kueue conditions\n\nDescription: Content-team deliverable (RHOAIUX-7470): final human-readable wording for the status message override table covering known Kueue condition/reason combinations, replacing engineering default copy. Raw Kueue message remains the fallback for unknown combos.\n\nScope:\n- Author override wording for known condition/reason combos (eviction reasons, requeued, admission check, WaitForRecovery vs WaitForStart, etc.)\n- Review with UXD (RHOAIUX-7470)\n- Deliver wording keyed to the override lookup structure for drop-in replacement\n\nACs:\n- Override copy covers all known condition/reason combinations recognized by the status model\n- Wording reviewed via RHOAIUX-7470\n- Unknown combinations still fall back to raw Kueue condition message (no blank states)\n\nHLR: supports P0-5, P2-2.\n\nE007 body:\n\nTitle: Documentation for Kueue workload scheduling visibility\n\nDescription: Docs deliverable: at minimum a release note for the Kueue scheduling visibility features; determine whether feature-level documentation is warranted and author it if so.\n\nScope:\n- Release note covering new status display, indicators, queue position, HP form changes\n- Determine if feature-level documentation is warranted; author if yes\n- Validate accuracy against implementation\n\nACs:\n- Release note published\n- Documentation-scope decision recorded with rationale\n- Any feature documentation technically reviewed against the implemented behavior\n- Accuracy validated against architecture context\