{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-58e3e5de-0401-43ba-b580-d0d0c9775b70","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-ac3e05501d0be02d","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8002-4yij0ax3/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8002-decomposition.md","content":"# Decomposition Summary: RHAISTRAT-8002\n\n## Integrate Kueue Workload Scheduling Information in Workbenches Overview\n\nStrategy: RHAISTRAT-8002 (Status: Release Pending, Priority: Major)\nComponent: odh-dashboard (canonical: **AI Core Dashboard** — see Component Mapping Notes)\n\n### Triage Decision\n\nBelow-threshold does not apply. The strategy is S-sized and affects a single component (odh-dashboard), but the multiple-distinct-work-streams escape condition fires: the scope spans (a) frontend code implementation, (b) substantive UX design authoring (RHOAIUX-7470 visual treatments), (c) substantive content authoring (status-message microcopy overrides), and (d) documentation (release note / possible feature docs). These are distinct work-product types owned by distinct teams (Dashboard UI, UXD, Content, Docs), each warranting its own review cycle. Not docs-only: odh-dashboard requires code changes.\n\n### Staff Engineer Input Overrides (traceability)\n\nThe Staff Engineer Input section is non-empty and takes precedence. Overrides applied:\n\n1. **rhods-operator removed from scope**: the HardwareProfile mutating webhook that injects the `kueue.x-k8s.io/queue-name` label is explicitly not part of this strategy. Only odh-dashboard frontend work remains.\n2. **Dependencies table replaced**: the only actual dependency is UXD finalized designs (RHOAIUX-7470), and development must NOT be blocked on it — placeholder copy/treatment during development, replace when UX delivers. Other listed dependencies were moved to Assumptions.\n3. **Scope constraints adopted**: quota/capacity preview is infeasible (LocalQueues carry no quota; ClusterQueue RBAC not guaranteed), estimated wait-time predictions, feature-flag model changes, opt-in/opt-out controls, queue management actions, and non-notebook workload types are all out of scope.\n4. **Status model direction**: state-driven from Workload CR conditions (not event-driven), `WorkloadCondition` type union corrected (no `Failed` type; failure is `Finished` with reason `Failed`), Preempted distinguished from other Eviction reasons.\n\n### Component Mapping Notes\n\n- `odh-dashboard` does not appear verbatim in `.context/rhai-components.txt`; mapped to canonical component **AI Core Dashboard** (closest match for the odh-dashboard frontend codebase).\n- Architecture context exists for odh-dashboard (`.context/architecture-context/architecture/rhoai-3.6-ea.1/odh-dashboard.md`) and for kueue-operator — component is in the platform; no onboarding chain (Rules 20) needed.\n- UXD epic mapped to canonical component **UXD**; documentation epic mapped to canonical component **Documentation**.\n\n### Open Questions Handling (Step 3)\n\nTwo open questions scanned; neither produces an Investigation epic because neither answer changes which epics exist or what they do:\n\n| Open question | Disposition | Rationale |\n|---|---|---|\n| Do data scientists receive RBAC aggregating `pending-workloads-lq-viewer-role`? | Acceptance criterion + validation note on the Visibility API epic | Code handles 403 gracefully either way; the implementation is identical regardless of the answer. Only the polish investment for position UI varies. |\n| What form should the positive Kueue indicator take (banner/badge/label)? | Placeholder treatment in the indicators epic; finalized design delivered by the UXD epic (RHOAIUX-7470) | Engineering effort is minimal regardless of choice; strategy explicitly mandates development is not blocked on UX answers. |\n\nNo conditional ADRs or pending reviews that gate epic structure. The RHOAIUX-7470 content review gates only the final wording/visuals, which are replacement deliverables over engineering defaults.\n\n## Epic List\n\n| ID | Title | Type | Team | Priority |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| RHAISTRAT-8002-E001 | State-driven Kueue workload status model and status display | Implementation | Dashboard UI | P0 |\n| RHAISTRAT-8002-E002 | Kueue Visibility API integration for queue position display | Implementation | Dashboard UI | P1 |\n| RHAISTRAT-8002-E003 | Kueue context indicators on project details and workbenches overview | Implementation | Dashboard UI | P0 |\n| RHAISTRAT-8002-E004 | HardwareProfile form and popover Kueue enhancements | Implementation | Dashboard UI | P1 |\n| RHAISTRAT-8002-E005 | UX visual treatment for Kueue indicators and status messaging (RHOAIUX-7470) | Implementation | UXD | P1 |\n| RHAISTRAT-8002-E006 | Human-friendly status message microcopy for Kueue conditions (RHOAIUX-7470) | Implementation | Content | P1 |\n| RHAISTRAT-8002-E007 | Documentation: release note and feature documentation determination | Implementation | Docs | P1 |\n\n## Dependency DAG\n\n```mermaid\ngraph TD\n    E001[\"E001 Status model (P0)\"] --> E002[\"E002 Visibility API position (P1)\"]\n    E001 --> E006[\"E006 Status microcopy (P1)\"]\n    E001 --> E007[\"E007 Documentation (P1)\"]\n    E002 --> E007\n    E003[\"E003 Kueue context indicators (P0)\"] --> E007\n    E004[\"E004 HP form/popover enhancements (P1)\"] --> E007\n    E005[\"E005 UX visual treatment (P1)\"] --> E007\n    E006 --> E007\n```\n\nCritical path: E001 → E006 → E007 (length 3).\n\n## DAG Justification\n\n| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n|---|---|---|\n| E001 → E002 | Rule 12 (framework → consumer) | The position display builds against the state-driven status model: pending state determination and the scheduling-status display surface it renders into are produced by the status model work. |\n| E001 → E006 | Rule 13 (artifact producer → consumer) | The status model work produces the override lookup structure and the enumerated condition/reason combinations; the microcopy deliverable slots into that structure. |\n| E001 → E007 | Rule 11 (docs-authoring always last) | Documentation blocked by all Implementation epics. |\n| E002 → E007 | Rule 11 | Same. |\n| E003 → E007 | Rule 11 | Same. |\n| E004 → E007 | Rule 11 | Same. |\n| E005 → E007 | Rule 11 | Same. |\n| E006 → E007 | Rule 11 | Same. |\n| No edge E005 → E003/E004 | Strategy constraint | Strategy explicitly mandates engineering is not blocked on UX answers; indicators ship with placeholder treatment and the finalized design replaces it. Parallel streams by design. |\n| No edges among E001, E003, E004 | Rule 15 | Same repo, different areas (status model vs. project-details/overview indicators vs. HP forms); no shared build-against artifacts — coordination risk only. |\n\n## HLR Traceability Matrix\n\n| HLR | Priority | Epic(s) |\n|---|---|---|\n| Distinguish Preempted from other Eviction reasons in workbench status display | P0 | E001 |\n| Surface Requeued state with retry count and next retry time from `requeueState` | P0 | E001 |\n| Positive Kueue indicator on project details page (`kueue.openshift.io/managed=true`) | P0 | E003 (finalized treatment: E005) |\n| Anomaly indicator on non-Kueue workloads in Kueue-managed namespaces | P0 | E003 (finalized treatment: E005) |\n| Workload scheduling status from Workload CR conditions with friendly overrides and raw fallback | P0 | E001 (final wording: E006) |\n| Kueue Visibility API queue position display with graceful 403 degradation | P1 | E002 |\n| HardwareProfile details popover fallback for GitOps-managed notebooks | P1 | E004 |\n| `k8sNameRegex` validation on LocalQueue name field in HP admin form | P1 | E004 |\n| Info indicator on HP dropdown explaining queue-enabled filtering | P1 | E004 (finalized treatment: E005) |\n| Structured, extensible status derivation model (no wildcard/substring event matching) | P2 | E001 |\n| Status message granularity: WaitForRecovery vs WaitForStart, AdmissionCheck states | P2 | E001 (final wording: E006) |\n\nAll 11 HLRs covered; no orphaned requirements. Non-functional requirements (backwards compatibility, graceful degradation, unknown-condition handling) are distributed as acceptance criteria across E001–E004.\n\n## Health Warnings\n\n1. **Priority note on UXD/Content epics (not an inversion, deliberate)**: E005 and E006 refine P0 features (indicators, status messages) but are P1. This follows the strategy's explicit direction that engineering ships P0 value with placeholder copy/treatment and the finalized UX/content deliverables replace placeholders afterward. Neither epic is a DAG prerequisite of the P0 engineering epics, so priority inheritance does not apply.\n2. **Effort estimate vs. epic count**: the strategy is S-sized (1–3 sprints) for the engineering core (E001–E004, all bounded odh-dashboard frontend work). The 7-epic count reflects cross-team work streams mandated by \"UXD Support is Required\" and \"Documentation Support is Required\", not engineering complexity.\n3. **RBAC open question downgraded to AC**: the Visibility API RBAC question was classified as an implementation-detail/validation item rather than a gating Investigation because the implementation (graceful 403 handling) is identical either way. If validation later finds `batch-user` RBAC is absent by default, position display silently becomes admin-only — a product-behavior change that needs no re-decomposition, only the documented finding.\n4. **Scope trap avoided**: the AI-generated \"Proposed Solution\" section lists extra UI (Resources column, historical data, queue details panel, estimated wait times). Per the Staff Engineer Input and the definitive HLR list, these are excluded — quota preview is technically infeasible (LocalQueues carry no quota) and estimated wait times are not provided by Kueue.\n\n## Tiered Delivery\n\nNo external dependency with uncertain timing exists (the Visibility API availability assumption is confirmed; no upstream PR/RFC is required). The internal UXD dependency (RHOAIUX-7470) is handled with the strategy's placeholder-and-replace pattern rather than tiered delivery: Tier-1-equivalent value (all engineering epics with default copy/treatment) ships without the UX deliverable; E005/E006/E007 complete the finalized experience afterward.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":59022,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-acec52fad2f4e93a","agent_id":"aa17cd262099402c2","session_id":"77a263a2-290e-4bf2-aaf1-488c79b76973","uuid":"454a3061-d25a-41a5-8a53-4c51d87df871","timestamp":"2026-10-22T10:30:08.664Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8002"}
