{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-d0185c33-54f4-46d8-88b0-bbae16cf0223","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-8d99ac7365064c9f","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8002-4yij0ax3/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8002-E001.md","content":"# State-driven Kueue workload status model and status display\n\n## Description\n\nRebuilds the workbench scheduling status display in the odh-dashboard frontend so that workload scheduling status is derived state-driven from Workload CR conditions and pod/container statuses, replacing the current event-driven model that matches hardcoded progress steps with wildcard/substring event matching. The status model distinguishes preemption from other eviction reasons, surfaces requeued/retry state, and guarantees that a human-readable message is always shown: a friendly override for known condition/reason combinations, with the raw Kueue condition message as an unconditional fallback. Under no circumstance does the UI show no information when a Kueue condition exists.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Extend the `WorkloadCondition` type union in `k8sTypes.ts`: remove the incorrect `'Failed'` entry (failure is expressed as `Finished` with reason `Failed`); include `QuotaReserved`, `Admitted`, `PodsReady`, `Finished`, `Evicted`, `Preempted`, `Requeued`, `BlockedOnPreemptionGates`, `DeactivationTarget`.\n- Replace wildcard/substring matching of events with a structured, extensible status derivation model driven by Workload CR conditions and pod/container statuses.\n- Distinguish \"Preempted\" (higher-priority workload took resources) from \"Evicted\" (admin action or timeout). Eviction reasons to handle include: Preempted, PodsReadyTimeout, AdmissionCheck, ClusterQueueStopped, LocalQueueStopped, Deactivated, NodeFailures, MaximumExecutionTimeExceeded.\n- Surface the Requeued state with retry count and next retry time computed from `requeueState` (including `requeueAt`) when a workload is evicted and waiting to re-enter the queue.\n- Provide human-friendly message overrides for known condition/reason combinations as a lookup table, with reasonable engineering-default copy; the fallback is always the raw Kueue condition `.message` field. Default copy must be structured for drop-in replacement when the finalized content deliverable arrives.\n- Improve status message granularity: distinguish WaitForRecovery from WaitForStart, and surface AdmissionCheck pending/retry states.\n- Unknown condition types or reasons must be shown with raw message text, never silently dropped.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given a Kueue-managed namespace where a workbench has been evicted due to `ClusterQueueStopped`, when the user views the workbench status, then the status displays \"Evicted\" with reason \"Queue stopped by administrator\" — NOT \"Preempted\", measured by the status label text and variant differing from the Preempted state.\n- Given a workbench has been evicted and the Workload CR has a `Requeued` condition with `requeueState.requeueAt` set, when the user views the workbench status, then the status displays the retry information including next retry time and attempt count, measured by the status text including the computed retry time from `requeueState`.\n- Given a workbench's Workload CR has a condition type or reason not recognized by the dashboard's status model, when the workbench status is rendered, then the raw Kueue condition message is displayed rather than a blank state, measured by the status text containing the Workload CR's condition `.message` field content.\n- Given a Workload CR contains condition types not yet in the dashboard's `WorkloadCondition` type union, when status is rendered, then the condition is shown with raw message text and never silently dropped (backwards compatibility).\n- All changes are purely additive and conditional: existing workbench behavior is unchanged when Kueue is not enabled or the namespace is not Kueue-managed.\n- The override lookup table uses placeholder default copy structured so the finalized wording can replace it without rework of the derivation logic.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- [P0] Distinguish Preempted from other Eviction reasons (ClusterQueueStopped, LocalQueueStopped, PodsReadyTimeout, Deactivated, etc.) in the workbench status display\n- [P0] Surface Requeued state with retry count and next retry time from `requeueState` when a workload is evicted and waiting to re-enter the queue\n- [P0] Display workload scheduling status derived from Workload CR conditions with human-friendly message overrides and raw message fallback\n- [P2] Improve status model progress steps to ensure all information related to workload scheduling is surfaced — move away from wildcard/substring matching of events to a structured, extensible status derivation model\n- [P2] Improve status message granularity: distinguish WaitForRecovery from WaitForStart, surface AdmissionCheck pending/retry states\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":62196,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-acec52fad2f4e93a","agent_id":"aa17cd262099402c2","session_id":"77a263a2-290e-4bf2-aaf1-488c79b76973","uuid":"c6331225-a6ae-4e93-b483-c740cba2a4c3","timestamp":"2026-10-22T10:30:28.109Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8002"}
