{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-1a5a55b4-7319-46e6-8df6-39ce4e70fcef","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-87d60af9d1185c50","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8002-4yij0ax3/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8002-E003.md","content":"# Kueue context indicators on project details and workbenches overview\n\n## Description\n\nAdds two conditional UI indicators to the odh-dashboard that communicate Kueue management context to users. First, a positive indicator on the project details page when the namespace is Kueue-managed, answering the question a user will inevitably ask when their workload does not start immediately. Second, an anomaly indicator on workbenches in Kueue-managed namespaces that are NOT managed by Kueue (missing the queue label) — serving the hybrid GitOps + dashboard user. Steady-state workloads that ARE Kueue-managed get no redundant \"managed by Kueue\" badge. Visual treatment ships with a placeholder that is replaced when the finalized UX design (RHOAIUX-7470) is delivered; engineering is not blocked on that design.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Project details page: positive indicator (info banner, badge, or label — exact form finalized by UX under RHOAIUX-7470; placeholder treatment during development) shown when the namespace has the `kueue.openshift.io/managed=true` label, stating that the project uses queue-based scheduling.\n- Workbenches overview: anomaly indicator shown ONLY on workbenches in a Kueue-managed namespace that are missing the `kueue.x-k8s.io/queue-name` label (created via GitOps or CLI bypassing the dashboard). Workload-to-Notebook matching uses the existing `buildWorkloadMapForNotebooks()` logic in `api/k8s/workloads.ts`.\n- The dashboard warns about missing queue labels but never blocks workload creation because of them.\n- Conditional display: all indicators appear only when the namespace is Kueue-managed; existing workbench behavior is unchanged otherwise (purely additive).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given a Kueue-managed namespace, when the user views the project details page, then a positive indicator is visible stating this project uses queue-based scheduling, measured by the indicator element being present in the DOM when the namespace label `kueue.openshift.io/managed=true` exists and absent when it does not.\n- Given a Kueue-managed namespace containing a workbench that does NOT have the `kueue.x-k8s.io/queue-name` label (created via GitOps or CLI without queue assignment), when the user views the workbenches overview, then that specific workbench displays a visual indicator that it is not managed by Kueue, measured by the anomaly indicator being present only on non-Kueue workloads and absent on Kueue-managed workloads.\n- The placeholder visual treatment is structured so the finalized UX design can replace it without rework of the conditional logic.\n- Existing workbench behavior is unchanged when the namespace is not Kueue-managed.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- [P0] Add positive Kueue indicator on project details page when namespace has `kueue.openshift.io/managed=true` label\n- [P0] Add anomaly indicator on workloads in a Kueue-managed namespace that are NOT managed by Kueue (missing `kueue.x-k8s.io/queue-name` label)\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":64207,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-acec52fad2f4e93a","agent_id":"aa17cd262099402c2","session_id":"77a263a2-290e-4bf2-aaf1-488c79b76973","uuid":"00109506-2d20-422b-9f39-f698f677a5a8","timestamp":"2026-10-22T10:30:51.451Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8002"}
