ce engineering placeholder treatments without rework of the conditional logic.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- The finalized visual treatment for the positive Kueue indicator is delivered, with the banner/badge/label decision recorded and rationale.\n- Visual designs for the workload anomaly indicator and the HP dropdown info indicator are delivered.\n- Status message content review (joint with the Content team under RHOAIUX-7470) is completed for the override wording.\n- Deliverables are specified against the implemented conditional behaviors so placeholder treatments can be swapped with minimal engineering rework.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- [P0] Add positive Kueue indicator on project details page when namespace has `kueue.openshift.io/managed=true` label (finalized visual treatment)\n- [P0] Add anomaly indicator on workloads in a Kueue-managed namespace that are NOT managed by Kueue (finalized visual treatment)\n- [P1] Add explicit info indicator on HP dropdown explaining why only queue-enabled profiles are shown in Kueue-managed namespaces (finalized visual treatment)\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":65999,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-acec52fad2f4e93a","agent_id":"aa17cd262099402c2","session_id":"77a263a2-290e-4bf2-aaf1-488c79b76973","uuid":"29376fa9-83b9-4661-a7fd-a32d9abd90f6","timestamp":"2026-10-22T10:31:15.182Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8002"}
