he status model's override table.\n- Wording is reviewed and approved via the RHOAIUX-7470 content review process.\n- Unknown condition/reason combinations continue to fall back to the raw Kueue condition `.message` text — the copy deliverable never introduces a blank state.\n- The delivered wording replaces the engineering defaults without rework of the status derivation logic.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- [P0] Display workload scheduling status derived from Workload CR conditions with human-friendly message overrides and raw message fallback (final override wording)\n- [P2] Improve status message granularity: distinguish WaitForRecovery from WaitForStart, surface AdmissionCheck pending/retry states (final wording)\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":66719,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-acec52fad2f4e93a","agent_id":"aa17cd262099402c2","session_id":"77a263a2-290e-4bf2-aaf1-488c79b76973","uuid":"2c945bcb-36f9-4fac-ae21-87d4886390c2","timestamp":"2026-10-22T10:31:24.305Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8002"}
