eviewed against the implemented behavior — accuracy validated against the actual implementation and the platform architecture context, not just the strategy text.\n- Documentation correctly states the conditional nature of the features (Kueue-managed namespaces only) and the graceful-degradation behaviors users may observe.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- All high level requirements of this strategy at the documentation level: P0 eviction-reason distinction, P0 requeued state, P0 positive Kueue indicator, P0 anomaly indicator, P0 status display with overrides, P1 Visibility API queue position, P1 HP popover fallback, P1 LocalQueue name validation, P1 HP dropdown info indicator, P2 structured status model, P2 status message granularity.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":67356,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-acec52fad2f4e93a","agent_id":"aa17cd262099402c2","session_id":"77a263a2-290e-4bf2-aaf1-488c79b76973","uuid":"c7b3ed6a-2d57-4023-8389-b11ebf9926aa","timestamp":"2026-10-22T10:31:34.386Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8002"}
