{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b3adddb830546455","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8002\n3\tepic_count: 7\n4\tcritical_path_length: 3\n5\tdecompose_complete: true\n6\ttriage: null\n7\ttriage_rationale: null\n8\t---\n9\t# Decomposition Summary: RHAISTRAT-8002\n10\t\n11\t## Integrate Kueue Workload Scheduling Information in Workbenches Overview\n12\t\n13\tStrategy: RHAISTRAT-8002 (Status: Release Pending, Priority: Major)\n14\tComponent: odh-dashboard (canonical: **AI Core Dashboard** — see Component Mapping Notes)\n15\t\n16\t### Triage Decision\n17\t\n18\tBelow-threshold does not apply. The strategy is S-sized and affects a single component (odh-dashboard), but the multiple-distinct-work-streams escape condition fires: the scope spans (a) frontend code implementation, (b) substantive UX design authoring (RHOAIUX-7470 visual treatments), (c) substantive content authoring (status-message microcopy overrides), and (d) documentation (release note / possible feature docs). These are distinct work-product types owned by distinct teams (Dashboard UI, UXD, Content, Docs), each warranting its own review cycle. Not docs-only: odh-dashboard requires code changes.\n19\t\n20\t### Staff Engineer Input Overrides (traceability)\n21\t\n22\tThe Staff Engineer Input section is non-empty and takes precedence. Overrides applied:\n23\t\n24\t1. **rhods-operator removed from scope**: the HardwareProfile mutating webhook that injects the `kueue.x-k8s.io/queue-name` label is explicitly not part of this strategy. Only odh-dashboard frontend work remains.\n25\t2. **Dependencies table replaced**: the only actual dependency is UXD finalized designs (RHOAIUX-7470), and development must NOT be blocked on it — placeholder copy/treatment during development, replace when UX delivers. Other listed dependencies were moved to Assumptions.\n26\t3. **Scope constraints adopted**: quota/capacity preview is infeasible (LocalQueues carry no quota; ClusterQueue RBAC not guaranteed), estimated wait-time predictions, feature-flag model changes, opt-in/opt-out controls, queue management actions, and non-notebook workload types are all out of scope.\n27\t4. **Status model direction**: state-driven from Workload CR conditions (not event-driven), `WorkloadCondition` type union corrected (no `Failed` type; failure is `Finished` with reason `Failed`), Preempted distinguished from other Eviction reasons.\n28\t\n29\t### Component Mapping Notes\n30\t\n31\t- `odh-dashboard` does not appear verbatim in `.context/rhai-components.txt`; mapped to canonical component **AI Core Dashboard** (closest match for the odh-dashboard frontend codebase).\n32\t- Architecture context exists for odh-dashboard (`.context/architecture-context/architecture/rhoai-3.6-ea.1/odh-dashboard.md`) and for kueue-operator — component is in the platform; no onboarding chain (Rules 20) needed.\n33\t- UXD epic mapped to canonical component **UXD**; documentation epic mapped to canonical component **Documentation**.\n34\t\n35\t### Open Questions Handling (Step 3)\n36\t\n37\tTwo open questions scanned; neither produces an Investigation epic because neither answer changes which epics exist or what they do:\n38\t\n39\t| Open question | Disposition | Rationale |\n40\t|---|---|---|\n41\t| Do data scientists receive RBAC aggregating `pending-workloads-lq-viewer-role`? | Acceptance criterion + validation note on the Visibility API epic | Code handles 403 gracefully either way; the implementation is identical regardless of the answer. Only the polish investment for position UI varies. |\n42\t| What form should the positive Kueue indicator take (banner/badge/label)? | Placeholder treatment in the indicators epic; finalized design delivered by the UXD epic (RHOAIUX-7470) | Engineering effort is minimal regardless of choice; strategy explicitly mandates development is not blocked on UX answers. |\n43\t\n44\tNo conditional ADRs or pending reviews that gate epic structure. The RHOAIUX-7470 content review gates only the final wording/visuals, which are replacement deliverables over engineering defaults.\n45\t\n46\t## Epic List\n47\t\n48\t| ID | Title | Type | Team | Priority |\n49\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n50\t| RHAISTRAT-8002-E001 | State-driven Kueue workload status model and status display | Implementation | Dashboard UI | P0 |\n51\t| RHAISTRAT-8002-E002 | Kueue Visibility API integration for queue position display | Implementation | Dashboard UI | P1 |\n52\t| RHAISTRAT-8002-E003 | Kueue context indicators on project details and workbenches overview | Implementation | Dashboard UI | P0 |\n53\t| RHAISTRAT-8002-E004 | HardwareProfile form and popover Kueue enhancements | Implementation | Dashboard UI | P1 |\n54\t| RHAISTRAT-8002-E005 | UX visual treatment for Kueue indicators and status messaging (RHOAIUX-7470) | Implementation | UXD | P1 |\n55\t| RHAISTRAT-8002-E006 | Human-friendly status message microcopy for Kueue conditions (RHOAIUX-7470) | Implementation | Content | P1 |\n56\t| RHAISTRAT-8002-E007 | Documentation: release note and feature documentation determination | Implementation | Docs | P1 |\n57\t\n58\t## Dependency DAG\n59\t\n60\t```mermaid\n61\tgraph TD\n62\t    E001[\"E001 Status model (P0)\"] --> E002[\"E002 Visibility API position (P1)\"]\n63\t    E001 --> E006[\"E006 Status microcopy (P1)\"]\n64\t    E001 --> E007[\"E007 Documentation (P1)\"]\n65\t    E002 --> E007\n66\t    E003[\"E003 Kueue context indicators (P0)\"] --> E007\n67\t    E004[\"E004 HP form/popover enhancements (P1)\"] --> E007\n68\t    E005[\"E005 UX visual treatment (P1)\"] --> E007\n69\t    E006 --> E007\n70\t```\n71\t\n72\tCritical path: E001 → E006 → E007 (length 3).\n73\t\n74\t## DAG Justification\n75\t\n76\t| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n77\t|---|---|---|\n78\t| E001 → E002 | Rule 12 (framework → consumer) | The position display builds against the state-driven status model: pending state determination and the scheduling-status display surface it renders into are produced by the status model work. |\n79\t| E001 → E006 | Rule 13 (artifact producer → consumer) | The status model work produces the override lookup structure and the enumerated condition/reason combinations; the microcopy deliverable slots into that structure. |\n80\t| E001 → E007 | Rule 11 (docs-authoring always last) | Documentation blocked by all Implementation epics. |\n81\t| E002 → E007 | Rule 11 | Same. |\n82\t| E003 → E007 | Rule 11 | Same. |\n83\t| E004 → E007 | Rule 11 | Same. |\n84\t| E005 → E007 | Rule 11 | Same. |\n85\t| E006 → E007 | Rule 11 | Same. |\n86\t| No edge E005 → E003/E004 | Strategy constraint | Strategy explicitly mandates engineering is not blocked on UX answers; indicators ship with placeholder treatment and the finalized design replaces it. Parallel streams by design. |\n87\t| No edges among E001, E003, E004 | Rule 15 | Same repo, different areas (status model vs. project-details/overview indicators vs. HP forms); no shared build-against artifacts — coordination risk only. |\n88\t\n89\t## HLR Traceability Matrix\n90\t\n91\t| HLR | Priority | Epic(s) |\n92\t|---|---|---|\n93\t| Distinguish Preempted from other Eviction reasons in workbench status display | P0 | E001 |\n94\t| Surface Requeued state with retry count and next retry time from `requeueState` | P0 | E001 |\n95\t| Positive Kueue indicator on project details page (`kueue.openshift.io/managed=true`) | P0 | E003 (finalized treatment: E005) |\n96\t| Anomaly indicator on non-Kueue workloads in Kueue-managed namespaces | P0 | E003 (finalized treatment: E005) |\n97\t| Workload scheduling status from Workload CR conditions with friendly overrides and raw fallback | P0 | E001 (final wording: E006) |\n98\t| Kueue Visibility API queue position display with graceful 403 degradation | P1 | E002 |\n99\t| HardwareProfile details popover fallback for GitOps-managed notebooks | P1 | E004 |\n100\t| `k8sNameRegex` validation on LocalQueue name field in HP admin form | P1 | E004 |\n101\t| Info indicator on HP dropdown explaining queue-enabled filtering | P1 | E004 (finalized treatment: E005) |\n102\t| Structured, extensible status derivation model (no wildcard/substring event matching) | P2 | E001 |\n103\t| Status message granularity: WaitForRecovery vs WaitForStart, AdmissionCheck states | P2 | E001 (final wording: E006) |\n104\t\n105\tAll 11 HLRs covered; no orphaned requirements. Non-functional requirements (backwards compatibility, graceful degradation, unknown-condition handling) are distributed as acceptance criteria across E001–E004.\n106\t\n107\t## Health Warnings\n108\t\n109\t1. **Priority note on UXD/Content epics (not an inversion, deliberate)**: E005 and E006 refine P0 features (indicators, status messages) but are P1. This follows the strategy's explicit direction that engineering ships P0 value with placeholder copy/treatment and the finalized UX/content deliverables replace placeholders afterward. Neither epic is a DAG prerequisite of the P0 engineering epics, so priority inheritance does not apply.\n110\t2. **Effort estimate vs. epic count**: the strategy is S-sized (1–3 sprints) for the engineering core (E001–E004, all bounded odh-dashboard frontend work). The 7-epic count reflects cross-team work streams mandated by \"UXD Support is Required\" and \"Documentation Support is Required\", not engineering complexity.\n111\t3. **RBAC open question downgraded to AC**: the Visibility API RBAC question was classified as an implementation-detail/validation item rather than a gating Investigation because the implementation (graceful 403 handling) is identical either way. If validation later finds `batch-user` RBAC is absent by default, position display silently becomes admin-only — a product-behavior change that needs no re-decomposition, only the documented finding.\n112\t4. **Scope trap avoided**: the AI-generated \"Proposed Solution\" section lists extra UI (Resources column, historical data, queue details panel, estimated wait times). Per the Staff Engineer Input and the definitive HLR list, these are excluded — quota preview is technically infeasible (LocalQueues carry no quota) and estimated wait times are not provided by Kueue.\n113\t\n114\t## Tiered Delivery\n115\t\n116\tNo external dependency with uncertain timing exists (the Visibility API availability assumption is confirmed; no upstream PR/RFC is required). The internal UXD dependency (RHOAIUX-7470) is handled with the strategy's placeholder-and-replace pattern rather than tiered delivery: Tier-1-equivalent value (all engineering epics with default copy/treatment) ships without the UX deliverable; E005/E006/E007 complete the finalized experience afterward.\n117\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a893d0885dac992a","agent_id":"a89fe66b116f94c03","session_id":"77a263a2-290e-4bf2-aaf1-488c79b76973","uuid":"f4451446-e4ee-4920-ba98-ee363afd26ec","timestamp":"2026-10-22T10:37:55.797Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b3adddb830546455","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-8002 decomposition"}
