{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9065f783742cf260","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8002-E006\n3\ttitle: Human-friendly status message microcopy for Kueue conditions (RHOAIUX-7470)\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8002\n5\tcomponent: AI Core Dashboard\n6\tteam: Content\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8002-E001\n11\tai_signals:\n12\t  change_specificity: 1\n13\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n14\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n15\t  existing_foundation: 1\n16\t  open_questions: 1\n17\t  external_dependency: 1\n18\t  human_process_gates: -1\n19\t  repo_access: 1\n20\t  architecture_claims: 0\n21\timplementation_type: null\n22\tinvestigation_signals: null\n23\tai_implementability: High\n24\tai_implementability_score: 4\n25\tjira_key: null\n26\tbranch: null\n27\tgated_by: null\n28\tgate_failure_impact: null\n29\t---\n30\t# Human-friendly status message microcopy for Kueue conditions (RHOAIUX-7470)\n31\t\n32\t## Description\n33\t\n34\tContent-team deliverable tracked under RHOAIUX-7470: final human-readable wording for the status message override table that maps known Kueue condition/reason combinations to friendly messages in the workbench status display. Raw Kueue condition messages are unintelligible to data scientists; this deliverable replaces the engineering default copy. Engineering is explicitly not blocked on it — reasonable defaults ship first and are replaced when content review is complete.\n35\t\n36\tThis work builds on the state-driven workload status model, which defines the override lookup structure and the enumerated set of known condition/reason combinations the wording must cover.\n37\t\n38\t## Scope\n39\t\n40\t- Author human-friendly message overrides for all known Kueue condition/reason combinations recognized by the status model, including: eviction reasons (Preempted, PodsReadyTimeout, AdmissionCheck, ClusterQueueStopped, LocalQueueStopped, Deactivated, NodeFailures, MaximumExecutionTimeExceeded), Requeued/retry states, AdmissionCheck pending/retry states, and the WaitForRecovery vs. WaitForStart distinction.\n41\t- Ensure wording targets non-Kubernetes users (data scientists) while remaining accurate to the underlying condition semantics.\n42\t- Complete content review with UXD under RHOAIUX-7470.\n43\t- Deliver the wording keyed to the override lookup structure so it drops in without changes to the derivation logic or the raw-message fallback.\n44\t\n45\t## Acceptance Criteria\n46\t\n47\t- Override copy covers every known condition/reason combination recognized by the status model's override table.\n48\t- Wording is reviewed and approved via the RHOAIUX-7470 content review process.\n49\t- Unknown condition/reason combinations continue to fall back to the raw Kueue condition `.message` text — the copy deliverable never introduces a blank state.\n50\t- The delivered wording replaces the engineering defaults without rework of the status derivation logic.\n51\t\n52\t## HLR Traceability\n53\t\n54\t- [P0] Display workload scheduling status derived from Workload CR conditions with human-friendly message overrides and raw message fallback (final override wording)\n55\t- [P2] Improve status message granularity: distinguish WaitForRecovery from WaitForStart, surface AdmissionCheck pending/retry states (final wording)\n56\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a893d0885dac992a","agent_id":"a89fe66b116f94c03","session_id":"77a263a2-290e-4bf2-aaf1-488c79b76973","uuid":"6d8f6434-2b80-48c6-9da8-d8a72e989b10","timestamp":"2026-10-22T10:38:03.062Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9065f783742cf260","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-8002 decomposition"}
