{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a4887d54f93532c4","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8002-E003\n3\ttitle: Kueue context indicators on project details and workbenches overview\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8002\n5\tcomponent: AI Core Dashboard\n6\tteam: Dashboard UI\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 1\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: 0\n16\t  external_dependency: 1\n17\t  human_process_gates: 0\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 6\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Kueue context indicators on project details and workbenches overview\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tAdds two conditional UI indicators to the odh-dashboard that communicate Kueue management context to users. First, a positive indicator on the project details page when the namespace is Kueue-managed, answering the question a user will inevitably ask when their workload does not start immediately. Second, an anomaly indicator on workbenches in Kueue-managed namespaces that are NOT managed by Kueue (missing the queue label) — serving the hybrid GitOps + dashboard user. Steady-state workloads that ARE Kueue-managed get no redundant \"managed by Kueue\" badge. Visual treatment ships with a placeholder that is replaced when the finalized UX design (RHOAIUX-7470) is delivered; engineering is not blocked on that design.\n34\t\n35\t## Scope\n36\t\n37\t- Project details page: positive indicator (info banner, badge, or label — exact form finalized by UX under RHOAIUX-7470; placeholder treatment during development) shown when the namespace has the `kueue.openshift.io/managed=true` label, stating that the project uses queue-based scheduling.\n38\t- Workbenches overview: anomaly indicator shown ONLY on workbenches in a Kueue-managed namespace that are missing the `kueue.x-k8s.io/queue-name` label (created via GitOps or CLI bypassing the dashboard). Workload-to-Notebook matching uses the existing `buildWorkloadMapForNotebooks()` logic in `api/k8s/workloads.ts`.\n39\t- The dashboard warns about missing queue labels but never blocks workload creation because of them.\n40\t- Conditional display: all indicators appear only when the namespace is Kueue-managed; existing workbench behavior is unchanged otherwise (purely additive).\n41\t\n42\t## Acceptance Criteria\n43\t\n44\t- Given a Kueue-managed namespace, when the user views the project details page, then a positive indicator is visible stating this project uses queue-based scheduling, measured by the indicator element being present in the DOM when the namespace label `kueue.openshift.io/managed=true` exists and absent when it does not.\n45\t- Given a Kueue-managed namespace containing a workbench that does NOT have the `kueue.x-k8s.io/queue-name` label (created via GitOps or CLI without queue assignment), when the user views the workbenches overview, then that specific workbench displays a visual indicator that it is not managed by Kueue, measured by the anomaly indicator being present only on non-Kueue workloads and absent on Kueue-managed workloads.\n46\t- The placeholder visual treatment is structured so the finalized UX design can replace it without rework of the conditional logic.\n47\t- Existing workbench behavior is unchanged when the namespace is not Kueue-managed.\n48\t\n49\t## HLR Traceability\n50\t\n51\t- [P0] Add positive Kueue indicator on project details page when namespace has `kueue.openshift.io/managed=true` label\n52\t- [P0] Add anomaly indicator on workloads in a Kueue-managed namespace that are NOT managed by Kueue (missing `kueue.x-k8s.io/queue-name` label)\n53\t"}]},"parent_tool_