{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-81dddbbd02ae1886","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8002-E004\n3\ttitle: HardwareProfile form and popover Kueue enhancements\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8002\n5\tcomponent: AI Core Dashboard\n6\tteam: Dashboard UI\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 1\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: 1\n16\t  external_dependency: 1\n17\t  human_process_gates: 1\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 8\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# HardwareProfile form and popover Kueue enhancements\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tHardens the HardwareProfile-related UI in the odh-dashboard for Kueue-managed contexts. The HP details popover correctly handles GitOps-managed notebooks whose queue label was applied directly (no matching HardwareProfile), the HP admin form validates LocalQueue names, the filtered HP dropdown in the workbench creation form explains why only queue-enabled profiles are shown, and workbench creation warns (but does not block) when a referenced LocalQueue does not exist in the target namespace.\n34\t\n35\t## Scope\n36\t\n37\t- HardwareProfile details popover: when no HP scheduling data exists for a notebook, fall back to reading the `kueue.x-k8s.io/queue-name` label from the notebook's own labels (a supported GitOps pattern). Resolve the cluster queue name from the project's LocalQueue list. Indicate the source: \"Queue: my-queue (applied directly)\" vs. \"Queue: my-queue (via hardware profile)\".\n38\t- HardwareProfile admin form: validate the LocalQueue name field against `k8sNameRegex` (`/^[a-z0-9]([-a-z0-9]*[a-z0-9])?$/`). Existence cannot be validated because HardwareProfiles are cluster-scoped while LocalQueues are namespace-scoped (target namespace unknown at HP creation time).\n39\t- Workbench creation form: if the specified LocalQueue does not exist in the target namespace, display a dismissible warning — NOT an error, and never blocking creation. The admin may have intended the LQ to be created later or delivered via GitOps; Kueue itself reports the error via the Workload's conditions if the queue truly does not exist.\n40\t- HardwareProfile dropdown in the workbench creation form (Kueue-managed namespaces): keep strict filtering to queue-enabled profiles only, and add an info icon or tooltip explaining \"Only queue-enabled hardware profiles are shown because this project uses queue-based scheduling.\" The principle: be opinionated, but tell users we are being opinionated.\n41\t\n42\t## Acceptance Criteria\n43\t\n44\t- Given a GitOps-managed workbench with `kueue.x-k8s.io/queue-name` label applied directly (no matching HardwareProfile), when the user opens the HardwareProfile details popover, then the popover displays the queue name with indication it was applied directly (not via hardware profile), measured by the popover text including the queue name and a source indicator.\n45\t- Given an admin is creating a HardwareProfile and enters an invalid LocalQueue name (e.g., contains uppercase or spaces), when the form validates, then a validation error is shown for the LocalQueue name field, measured by the form displaying an inline error referencing the Kubernetes name format.\n46\t- Given a workbench is being created with a HardwareProfile referencing a LocalQueue that does not exist in the target namespace, when the creation form is submitted, then a warning (not error) is displayed indicating the local queue was not found, measured by the warning being dismissible and not blocking workbench creation.\n47\t- Given a workbench is in a Kueue-managed namespace and the user opens the workbench creation form, when the HardwareProfile dropdown renders with only queue-enabled profiles, then an info indicator explains why only queue-enabled profiles are shown, measured by the presence of a tooltip or info icon adjacent to the dropdown.\n48\t- All changes are conditional on Kueue-managed context; behavior in non-Kueue namespaces is unchanged.\n49\t\n50\t## HLR Traceability\n51\t\n52\t- [P1] Fix HardwareProfile details popover for GitOps-managed notebooks: read queue label directly when no HP match exists, indicate source\n53\t- [P1] Add `k8sNameRegex` validation to LocalQueue name field in HardwareProfile admin form\n54\t- [P1] Add explicit info indicator on HP dropdown explaining why only queue-enabled profiles are shown in Kueue-managed namespaces\n55\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a893d0885dac992a","agent_id":"a89fe66b116f94c03","session_id":"77a263a2-290e-4bf2-aaf1-488c79b76973","uuid":"6b3aa77f-6f11-46b7-901a-bfa200a2b831","timestamp":"2026-10-22T10:38:18.766Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-81dddbbd02ae1886","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-8002 decomposition"}
