{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b42cc8e5dc4f5394","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8002-E002\n3\ttitle: Kueue Visibility API integration for queue position display\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8002\n5\tcomponent: AI Core Dashboard\n6\tteam: Dashboard UI\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8002-E001\n11\tai_signals:\n12\t  change_specificity: 1\n13\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n14\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n15\t  existing_foundation: 1\n16\t  open_questions: 0\n17\t  external_dependency: 1\n18\t  human_process_gates: 1\n19\t  repo_access: 1\n20\t  architecture_claims: 1\n21\timplementation_type: null\n22\tinvestigation_signals: null\n23\tai_implementability: High\n24\tai_implementability_score: 7\n25\tjira_key: null\n26\tbranch: null\n27\tgated_by: null\n28\tgate_failure_impact: null\n29\t---\n30\t# Kueue Visibility API integration for queue position display\n31\t\n32\t## Description\n33\t\n34\tIntegrates Kueue's Visibility API (aggregated API server, API group `visibility.kueue.x-k8s.io`) into the odh-dashboard workbenches overview so that queue position is displayed for pending workloads. Queue position is not a field on the Workload object — it lives on the `PendingWorkload` type served via the Visibility API's `PendingWorkloadsSummary` subresource on LocalQueues. All Kubernetes API calls use the logged-in user's token through the existing `/api/k8s` passthrough proxy and are subject to the user's RBAC. Position info is supplementary: a 403 on the Visibility API must fail silently.\n35\t\n36\tThis work depends on the state-driven workload status model (which determines pending state and provides the scheduling-status display surface the position renders into); it builds on that model rather than replicating it.\n37\t\n38\t## Scope\n39\t\n40\t- Fetch queue position data via the LocalQueue pendingworkloads subresource: `GET /apis/visibility.kueue.x-k8s.io/v1beta2/namespaces/{ns}/localqueues/{name}/pendingworkloads`, using the logged-in user's token via the `/api/k8s` passthrough proxy.\n41\t- Display `positionInLocalQueue` (and `positionInClusterQueue` where available to the user) for workloads in QueuingPending state in the workbenches overview.\n42\t- Graceful degradation on 403 using the existing `getGenericErrorCode` pattern from `DistributedWorkloadsContext.tsx`: position info is silently omitted, no error is displayed.\n43\t- Validate whether the `pending-workloads-lq-viewer-role` ClusterRole (aggregated to `batch-user`, `view`, `admin`, `edit`) is effectively granted to data scientists in RHOAI clusters by default, and document the finding. The implementation handles 403 correctly either way; the finding determines whether position display is broadly available or effectively admin-only, and informs position UI polish investment.\n44\t\n45\t## Acceptance Criteria\n46\t\n47\t- Given a workbench is in QueuingPending state and the user's token has `batch-user` RBAC to the Visibility API, when the workbenches overview page renders, then the queue position is displayed (position in local queue), measured by the position number being present and matching the value from the `pendingworkloads` subresource.\n48\t- Given a workbench is in QueuingPending state and the user's token does NOT have RBAC to the Visibility API, when the workbenches overview page renders, then the queue position is silently omitted with no error displayed, measured by the absence of both position data and error indicators.\n49\t- The RBAC availability validation finding is documented; behavior is correct (graceful degradation) regardless of the outcome.\n50\t- UI remains responsive with the Kueue Visibility API integration (performance success criterion).\n51\t- The workbenches overview handles large numbers of queued workloads (scalability success criterion): given a Kueue-managed namespace with a large volume of pending workloads (100+ entries returned across the namespace's LocalQueue `pendingworkloads` subresources), the overview renders queue position and scheduling status for every pending workbench with no dropped, blank, or stale status entries, measured by all pending workbench rows displaying position/status data consistent with the subresource values under that volume.\n52\t- Only factual queue position data is displayed — no estimated wait time predictions (Kueue does not provide them).\n53\t\n54\t## HLR Traceability\n55\t\n56\t- [P1] Integrate Kueue Visibility API for queue position display (`positionInLocalQueue`, `positionInClusterQueue`) via `PendingWorkloadsSummary` subresource on LocalQueue — gracefully degrade on 403\n57\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b7a3dd601a276d44","agent_id":"a2fe83627be0e5be3","session_id":"77a263a2-290e-4bf2-aaf1-488c79b76973","uuid":"6d42c927-a95d-4613-98b1-38b2f370841e","timestamp":"2026-10-22T10:40:07.504Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b42cc8e5dc4f5394","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8002 decomposition"}
