Kueue-managed (missing queue label) — distinct from steady-state \"managed by Kueue\" affordances, which are deliberately absent.\n39\t- Design the info indicator / tooltip treatment for the HardwareProfile dropdown that explains why only queue-enabled profiles are shown in Kueue-managed namespaces (\"be opinionated, but tell users we are being opinionated\").\n40\t- Collaborate on content review of the human-friendly status message overrides for Kueue conditions (joint UXD/Content review under RHOAIUX-7470).\n41\t- Deliver design specs structured so they can replace engineering placeholder treatments without rework of the conditional logic.\n42\t\n43\t## Acceptance Criteria\n44\t\n45\t- The finalized visual treatment for the positive Kueue indicator is delivered, with the banner/badge/label decision recorded and rationale.\n46\t- Visual designs for the workload anomaly indicator and the HP dropdown info indicator are delivered.\n47\t- Status message content review (joint with the Content team under RHOAIUX-7470) is completed for the override wording.\n48\t- Deliverables are specified against the implemented conditional behaviors so placeholder treatments can be swapped with minimal engineering rework.\n49\t\n50\t## HLR Traceability\n51\t\n52\t- [P0] Add positive Kueue indicator on project details page when namespace has `kueue.openshift.io/managed=true` label (finalized visual treatment)\n53\t- [P0] Add anomaly indicator on workloads in a Kueue-managed namespace that are NOT managed by Kueue (finalized visual treatment)\n54\t- [P1] Add explicit info indicator on HP dropdown explaining why only queue-enabled profiles are shown in Kueue-managed namespaces (finalized visual treatment)\n55\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b7a3dd601a276d44","agent_id":"a2fe83627be0e5be3","session_id":"77a263a2-290e-4bf2-aaf1-488c79b76973","uuid":"8e95d02e-0f5c-4f07-89f4-d7933fb076bb","timestamp":"2026-10-22T10:40:10.465Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b600115dd0f431e