ing).\n44\t- Determine whether feature-level documentation is warranted for the Kueue scheduling visibility capabilities and record the decision with rationale; author feature documentation if warranted.\n45\t- Document the user-facing behavior boundaries: indicators and status information appear only in Kueue-managed namespaces; queue position may be absent for users without Visibility API RBAC; estimated wait times are not provided.\n46\t\n47\t## Acceptance Criteria\n48\t\n49\t- A release note covering all user-visible changes in this strategy is published.\n50\t- The decision on feature-level documentation (warranted or not) is recorded with rationale; if warranted, the feature documentation is authored.\n51\t- All documentation is technically reviewed against the implemented behavior — accuracy validated against the actual implementation and the platform architecture context, not just the strategy text.\n52\t- Documentation correctly states the conditional nature of the features (Kueue-managed namespaces only) and the graceful-degradation behaviors users may observe.\n53\t\n54\t## HLR Traceability\n55\t\n56\t- All high level requirements of this strategy at the documentation level: P0 eviction-reason distinction, P0 requeued state, P0 positive Kueue indicator, P0 anomaly indicator, P0 status display with overrides, P1 Visibility API queue position, P1 HP popover fallback, P1 LocalQueue name validation, P1 HP dropdown info indicator, P2 structured status model, P2 status message granularity.\n57\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b7a3dd601a276d44","agent_id":"a2fe83627be0e5be3","session_id":"77a263a2-290e-4bf2-aaf1-488c79b76973","uuid":"d1f5672b-1c87-4752-9113-a0fed5ed88b8","timestamp":"2026-10-22T10:40:12.122Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8c797b0f23bd5e7f","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8002 decomposition"}
